var e={tool:`podman CLI`,download:`https://podman.io/docs/installation`,guide:`https://docs.podman.io/en/latest/markdown/podman-port.1.html`,setup:{windows:`Follow Podman's Windows installation and machine setup; containers use a WSLv2-backed guest.`,darwin:`Use the official installer and explicitly initialize/start a Podman machine when needed.`,linux:`Use the documented distribution package; rootless operation can need local setup.`},afterSetup:`Inspect an existing container's mapping with native Podman, then set the HTTP draft to the real local port. A located CLI does not prove its machine is started.`,notes:[`This guide does not create or start machines, contact Podman, pull images or run containers.`,`Keep local services bound to loopback. A guest port can differ from its host mapping.`],commands:[{label:`Example: inspect existing mapped ports`,text:`podman port example-container`}],endpoint:{url:`http://127.0.0.1:8080/`,notice:`Example host HTTP port. Confirm your running container/machine and its actual port mapping before Send.`}};export{e as default};